## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical skills in cross-DC coordination, configuration management, and state synchronization using Docker Config and Redis Pub/Sub. It also covers rate limiting and error handling under load.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for storing per-tenant quota limits
- Redis PUB/SUB for cross-DC quota propagation
- Quota checks with eventual consistency across peers
- TLS edge routing with Traefik

## Code Example
```javascript
const quota = getQuota(tenantId);
if (quota <= 0) throw new Error('Quota exceeded');

await performImport(data);
decrementQuota(tenantId);
publishQuotaUpdate(tenantId, getQuota(tenantId));
```

## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests the ability to design per-tenant traffic control across data centers, implement dynamic configuration updates, and establish observability—all without service downtime.

## Key Concepts
- **Deterministic hashing**: Ensures consistent per-tenant canary decisions across all service instances
- **Docker Config**: Enables dynamic configuration reloads and zero-downtime rollouts
- **Multi-DC routing**: Traefik handles TLS termination with per-tenant observability across both data centers

## Code Example
```javascript
function isCanary(tenant, percentage) {
  const hash = [...tenant].reduce((acc, char) => (acc * 31 + char.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0, 0);
  return (hash % 100) < percentage;
}
```
